  "text": "Recipe: Aloo Tikki Chaat\nCreator: Shalini Priyadarshini\nCategory: Chaat\nIngredients: potatoes, kala chana (brown chickpeas), cilantro, salt, soy yogurt, red Kashmiri chilli powder, green chillies, roasted cumin powder, tamarind, dates\nCooking methods: saute, no-cook\nInstructions: + ALOO TIKKI: Combine boiled potatoes & boiled kala chana (brown chickpeas) in approximately 1:1 ratio. Add some cilantro and a pinch of salt (to taste). Mash them together. Shape them into burger patties or 'tikkis'. Cook on a preheated cast iron tawa on medium low heat until both sides are crispy.\n+ ALOO TIKKI CHAAT: Put Aloo Tikki on a plate. Spread some lightly beaten soy yogurt. Add some red Kashmiri chilli powder, chopped green chillies, roasted cumin powder and a pinch of salt (to taste). Garnish with chopped cilantro and homemade Tamarind Date Chutney.\nNotes: A recipe with BEANS (kala chana, soy yogurt), TUBERS (potatoes), HERBS & SPICES (various). Homemade Tamarind Date Chutney is a component.",
